Well I had a great game going. Figured I was on my way to a YAFAP and was
already planning my celebration. This game tought be something new about
getting protection from priests, and I had took my time to gather and alter
test all dropped armor so I had a -20 ac. I had not found any speical armor
till the mirror on Medusa's level. I started using Hearse about midway
through the game, didn't know that it would affect a game in progress. I was
granted Mjollnier and somebody elses bones file had a cursed vorpal blade
and a +2 frostbrand.

I forgot to do sokoban, sort of. I started it, but screwed up on several of
it's levels so read both scrolls of earth and broke a large number of
boulders. So I decided not to do the zoo at the end till my luck timed out.
I didn't remember to go back till I had reached Medusa and I wanted more
protection so I returned to sokoban. This leads me to my first question.
I've noticed that many times the zoo in sokoban has a co-alinged unicorn. I
can't remember if there is always one there, so is there? In anycase it
allowed me to identify all of my gens.

Medusa proved to be no problem although there was a master mindflayer
stranded on an island that I avoided. I descended to the castle and
encountered my first master lich. I cancled him but he could still cast
spells, he summoned several times but my armor class proved to be high
enough to keep those down to a minor threat. I managed to drive the master
lich upstairs and went around to the back of the castle. The dragons proved
to be no problem but the gave no scales. Then I scoured the treasury and
found some interesting gloves. I decided to go back up to an altar to see
what I could see. But alas I forgot to put my ring of levitation on, and
fell into the valley of the dead. This proved to be no big deal, and even
netted me a wraith corpse. I found the temple there and the stairs up and
continued up. Well to make a long story short that master lich was waiting
for me. I battled him on several occasions and then teleported to the room
with the stairs to finnish him off. He summoned up a group of nasties and
disintegrated my boots in this last fight. But I saw an end to this hard
fight. He summoned a cockatrice, which died easily to my +6 frostbrand. I
moved over and picked up the corpse...DYWYPI

What could I have done differently.
Well I still had a few unidentified scrolls that I could have identified
before descending. There could have been a genocide scroll in there.
I could have invoked the Orb of Fate. I did have teleport control and was on
a level that I could teleport on.
I could have paid more attention to the boots dissapearing message and
checked my equipment before picking up the cockatrice corpse.

Otherwise the game was probably the best game I had ever played in terms of
technique. I found very little of the equipment I would normaly have before
going this deep. Guantlets of power, speed boots, reflection(which I did get
from Perseus), magic resistance. But none the less my character still did
extremely well. I didn't run a protection racket per say but I did wait to
drink potions of gain level till after I had bought most of it.
I used no wishes, but I would have if I had the chance.
I used no genocide, but once again I would of if I had the chance.



